---
// Privacy policy. Written plain-English and first person to match the rest of the
// site. Every claim here must stay in sync with the app's actual behavior and the
// App Store privacy labels. Linked from the footer and from the landing page's
// privacy section ("See exactly what's shared" -> #whats-shared).
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { site, links, withBase } from "../data/site";

const effectiveDate = "July 5, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title={`Privacy Policy — ${site.name}`} description={`How ${site.name} handles your data: no accounts, no tracking, and card recognition that runs entirely on your device.`}>
  <main class="flex-grow w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto px-page-margin py-16 flex flex-col gap-10">
    <a
      class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors font-label-md self-start"
      href={withBase("/")}>← Back to Gather Scanner</a
    >

    <header class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h1 class="text-display font-display text-on-surface">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-label-sm font-label-sm text-text-muted">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Plain-English summary -->
    <section class="bg-surface-elevated p-6 rounded-2xl border border-surface-border flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">The short version</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Gather Scanner has no accounts and doesn't track you. Your collection lives on your
        phone, and card recognition runs entirely on the device. The only information the app
        ever sends anywhere is a scan correction you explicitly choose to share, and that's
        off by default. Everything below is the detail behind those sentences.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">What does use the network</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        A few things require an internet connection. None of them send information about you or
        your collection:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 flex flex-col gap-2 text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-on-surface">Card data and price updates.</strong> At app start,
          Gather Scanner downloads the latest card database and price list from GitHub Releases.
          This is a plain file download: no additional information is sent. Like
          any web request, GitHub's servers see your IP address, covered by
          <a class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors" href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-on-surface">Purchases.</strong> The one-time unlock is processed
          entirely by Apple through the App Store. I never see your payment details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-on-surface">Crash reports.</strong> If you've opted in to sharing
          crash data with developers in your iOS settings, Apple provides anonymized crash
          reports. There is no third-party crash or analytics SDK in the app.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-on-surface">Opt-in scan corrections.</strong> Described in full
          below.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3 scroll-mt-24" id="whats-shared">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Opt-in scan corrections: exactly what's shared</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        When the scanner gets a card wrong and you correct it, you can choose to share that
        correction to improve recognition for everyone. This is <strong class="text-on-surface">off by default</strong>
        and you can turn it off anytime in settings. If you opt in, each shared correction contains
        exactly three things:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 flex flex-col gap-2 text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        <li>A close-up crop of the scanned card image. (Only the area inside the highlighted frame is shared.)</li>
        <li>The card the scanner identified it as.</li>
        <li>The card you corrected it to.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Corrections contain no device identifier, email, location, or anything about the
        rest of your collection. They're stored on my server and used only to train and improve
        card recognition, in Gather Scanner and in related products I may build. They are never
        sold or shared with anyone else. Because submissions are anonymous, I have no way to connect a
        stored correction back to you, which also means I can't retrieve or delete a specific
        person's submissions on request. If that gives you pause, leave sharing off; the scanner
        works identically either way.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Gather Scanner doesn't collect your data</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 flex flex-col gap-2 text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        <li>No accounts, sign-ins, or email addresses. There's nothing to sign up for.</li>
        <li>No analytics or advertising SDKs, and no ads.</li>
        <li>No tracking of what you scan, own, or search for.</li>
        <li>Your collection is never uploaded to a server. It stays on your device and in your normal device backups, under your control.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Your collection is yours</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Everything you scan and organize is stored on your device. You can export your full
        collection at any time, and deleting the app deletes its data from your device (your own
        iOS backups are governed by your device settings). There is no server-side copy for me to
        keep, share, or lose.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        If the app's behavior changes in a way that affects your privacy, this page will be
        updated and the effective date above will change before that behavior ships. Any such
        change will also coincide with an app update and a notification inside the app, so you
        won't have to re-read this page to find out something changed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Questions</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Email <a class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors" href={links.support}>support@gatherscanner.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
